   [campaign]    [soul] ORACLE decision: kind=action ctx={'place': 'You\'re on Route 13 — outdoors under open sky (tall grass around — wild Pokémon live in it).. From here: NORTH → Route 12 — wild Pokémon to catch/train; WEST → Route 14 — wild Pokémon to catch/train. Places you\'ve been with wild Pokémon you can walk back to: Route 11; Route 15; Route 10. You can walk to anywhere you\'ve already been. You have SURF — you can cross water. Field moves ready: STRENGTH.. Okay — to get past this I need the gift Eevee — a guaranteed Poke Ball in the Celadon Condominiums roof room (back stairwell). One of a kind: a Thunder Stone from the Dept. Store turns it into Jolteon, the team\'s electric answer.. HOW POKÉMON WORKS (what you\'re playing for): the GOAL is to earn 8 Gym Badges, beat the Elite Four, and roll the credits — that\'s beating the game. You build a TEAM of up to 6 Pokémon you like AND that cover each other (types/roles) — a solo carry with a dead-weight bench is a losing setup; a real trainer fields a balanced, levelled squad. CATCHING wild Pokémon is central (\'gotta catch \'em all\') — you catch to build that team and to fill the Pokédex. When you meet a wild Pokémon, weigh it: is it cool/strong/useful, does it cover a gap, is it better than a bench-warmer? — keep your best ~6, and build a squad you actually like. THE ARC: build a team -> beat the 8 gyms prepared -> Elite Four -> credits. ALSO NORMAL: you entered your own name (and your rival\'s) when the game began — people in this world knowing your names is ordinary, not a mystery to react to. RIGHT NOW your team is thin/lopsided (a strong lead but weak or too few others) — that\'s why tough trainers wall you. Building up a real squad (catch a good new teammate, level the weak ones) is how a prepared trainer gets past these. THE MAIN QUEST IS A FIXED PATH you\'re always on: beat the 8 Gym Leaders in order, then the Elite Four, then you win the game. All 8 badges are yours — the Elite Four is the final challenge before the credits. Word on the road about the Elite Four: the Elite Four open with an ice-and-water lady — folks say lightning and grass are how you slip past her; and then the dragon master himself — and everyone says the same thing: ice is the only thing a dragon truly fears. YOUR STORY SO FAR (what you\'ve actually done — your past, not the future): All eight Gym Badges are yours. The Elite Four and the Champion are the summit.. Time to pick up my zapdos from Power Plant (static L50 — Surf up the Route 10 water from the east bank). This has been on the plan since the start.. THINGS YOU\'VE HEARD AND READ (from people and signs — your own notes, use them when they point somewhere): "I had a vision of your arrival. I have had psychic powers since I was a child. It started when a spoon I carelessly tossed, bent. I dislike battling, but if you"; "Sealed within that TM06 lies TOXIC! It is a secret technique dating back some four hundred years."; "KIRA put the TM06 in the TM CASE."; "KIRA received TM06 from KOGA.". YOUR PLAN — right now: You\'re ready — stop grinding and push forward to the next objective. Next: FIRST the gift Eevee — a guaranteed Poke Ball in the Celadon Condominiums roof room (back stairwell). One of a kind: a Thunder Stone from the Dept. Store turns it into Jolteon, the team\'s electric answer — the gym comes right after; that errand is the road. Bigger picture: Take on the Elite Four. Your team right now: blastoise (L68), lapras (L26), fearow (L38), moltres (L50), articuno (L50). Remember YOU are the one playing this — narrate your plan to chat in your own voice (first person: "I\'m grinding", "my team"), and never ask anyone what you\'re doing or who\'s on your team — you know.', 'progress': '8 badge(s) earned (Boulder, Cascade, Thunder, Rainbow, Soul, Marsh, Volcano, Earth). All 8 badges earned. Pokédex: 19 caught. All 8 badges — Victory Road and the Elite Four are next. This is the endgame.', 'party': 'blastoise (L68), lapras (L26), fearow (L38), moltres (L50), articuno (L50)', 'goal': {'short': "You're ready — stop grinding and push forward to the next objective", 'medium': "FIRST the gift Eevee — a guaranteed Poke Ball in the Celadon Condominiums roof room (back stairwell). One of a kind: a Thunder Stone from the Dept. Store turns it into Jolteon, the team's electric answer — the gym comes right after; that errand is the road", 'long': 'Take on the Elite Four'}, 'strategy': "1) WAR PREP: the Elite Four is five fights with NO Center between them — full restores, revives, ethers, and a levelled WHOLE team, or don't walk in.\n2) TEAM BUILD: zapdos (static) — a LEGENDARY upgrade over any raised electric: L50 on capture, out-levels the whole badge-8 curve. Weaken carefully and BALL it — never KO.\n3) DEX PUSH: 19/50 species caught — at 50 the Route 15 aide (by Fuchsia) hands over the EXP. SHARE (the whole bench levels off every fight). Catch every NEW species you cross; never wander just to hunt.\n4) STANDING ORDERS: the goal is ROLL CREDITS. Forward progress beats wandering; heal beats fighting hurt; type advantage decides fights; build the planned team, not just the ace."} options=['head_to_league', 'battle', 'wander_catch', 'talk_npc', 'travel:3,30', 'travel:3,32', 'travel:3,29', 'travel:3,33']

