r, then the Elite Four, then you win the game. All 8 badges are yours — the Elite Four is the final challenge before the credits. Word on the road about the Elite Four: the Elite Four open with an ice-and-water lady — folks say lightning and grass are how you slip past her; and then the dragon master himself — and everyone says the same thing: ice is the only thing a dragon truly fears. YOUR STORY SO FAR (what you\'ve actually done — your past, not the future): All eight Gym Badges are yours. The Elite Four and the Champion are the summit.. Time to pick up my zapdos from Power Plant (static L50 — Surf up the Route 10 water from the east bank). This has been on the plan since the start.. THINGS YOU\'VE HEARD AND READ (from people and signs — your own notes, use them when they point somewhere): "I had a vision of your arrival. I have had psychic powers since I was a child. It started when a spoon I carelessly tossed, bent. I dislike battling, but if you"; "Sealed within that TM06 lies TOXIC! It is a secret technique dating back some four hundred years."; "KIRA put the TM06 in the TM CASE."; "KIRA received TM06 from KOGA.". YOUR PLAN — right now: You\'re ready — stop grinding and push forward to the next objective. Next: FIRST the gift Eevee — a guaranteed Poke Ball in the Celadon Condominiums roof room (back stairwell). One of a kind: a Thunder Stone from the Dept. Store turns it into Jolteon, the team\'s electric answer — the gym comes right after; that errand is the road. Bigger picture: Take on the Elite Four. Your team right now: blastoise (L68), lapras (L26), fearow (L38), moltres (L50), articuno (L50). Remember YOU are the one playing this — narrate your plan to chat in your own voice (first person: "I\'m grinding", "my team"), and never ask anyone what you\'re doing or who\'s on your team — you know.', 'progress': '8 badge(s) earned (Boulder, Cascade, Thunder, Rainbow, Soul, Marsh, Volcano, Earth). All 8 badges earned. Pokédex: 19 caught. All 8 badges — Victory Road and the Elite Four are next. This is the endgame.', 'party': 'blastoise (L68), lapras (L26), fearow (L38), moltres (L50), articuno (L50)', 'goal': {'short': "You're ready — stop grinding and push forward to the next objective", 'medium': "FIRST the gift Eevee — a guaranteed Poke Ball in the Celadon Condominiums roof room (back stairwell). One of a kind: a Thunder Stone from the Dept. Store turns it into Jolteon, the team's electric answer — the gym comes right after; that errand is the road", 'long': 'Take on the Elite Four'}, 'strategy': "1) WAR PREP: the Elite Four is five fights with NO Center between them — full restores, revives, ethers, and a levelled WHOLE team, or don't walk in.\n2) TEAM BUILD: zapdos (static) — a LEGENDARY upgrade over any raised electric: L50 on capture, out-levels the whole badge-8 curve. Weaken carefully and BALL it — never KO.\n3) DEX PUSH: 19/50 species caught — at 50 the Route 15 aide (by Fuchsia) hands over the EXP. SHARE (the whole bench levels off every fight). Catch every NEW species you cross; never wander just to hunt.\n4) STANDING ORDERS: the goal is ROLL CREDITS. Forward progress beats wandering; heal beats fighting hurt; type advantage decides fights; build the planned team, not just the ace."} options=['head_to_league', 'battle', 'wander_catch', 'talk_npc', 'travel:3,30', 'travel:3,32', 'travel:3,29', 'travel:3,33']



